From bf810a317403f13866d9c241aea32592cfe9e561 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:19:53 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add a game switcher and an activity page, and count play time
 awake

FN + SELECT shows the recent games one at a time, each with the screenshot of its automatic
save state, and A continues where it stopped. During a game the kit's guard closes a game
that writes its automatic state and the menu opens the switcher when it is back; the menu
tells the guard which games those are. START > Canica gains the switcher and an activity
page: total time, games and plays, the last seven days, streaks, the most played games and
the favourite hour and day, from the menu's game time and a log of sessions. A game's time
now counts only while the console is awake, so a suspended game adds nothing. The three
terminal screens share their style and drawing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
